CVE-2025-29927: Next.js middleware authorization bypass via x-middleware-subrequest.

Re-authored against the compiled npm artifact (next@14.2.10 ships prebuilt
JavaScript under dist/, not the monorepo TypeScript sources). Ports the
prerequisite filterInternalHeaders/INTERNAL_HEADERS helper into 14.2.10 and
layers the CVE fix: a per-session middlewareSubrequestId is generated with
crypto.getRandomValues and the spoofable x-middleware-subrequest header is
stripped from external requests unless it carries the matching session id.
Applied to both the CJS (dist/) and ESM (dist/esm/) builds. Upstream fix:
vercel/next.js 52a078da (#77201) / 5fd3ae8f (#77202 v14 backport).

